# {name}

Say here how to use {name} well: what to call first, what to store and what to do when it fails. Apps read this with
`jadpo package show {snake} --guide`.

## Before you release it

Delete this section when these are done.

1. Replace the `starter` library, its types, its failure and the `tidy_entered_text` recipe with your own. `jadpo package check` runs the
   publishing bar on the package whenever you want to know where it stands.
2. Say what the package does in `package.jadpo`'s description, and why it is
   released in `CHANGELOG.md`.
3. To publish it to the public registry, choose an open licence in
   `package.jadpo` and name your handle as `publisher:`. A package only used
   by path or from git may stay `Licence.proprietary`, with no publisher.
4. Commit it, run `jadpo package check` and tag the commit `v1.0.0`.
